From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: Hide Trek Tech article formatting markers

Some Trek Tech article paragraphs begin with a legacy 0xA5 formatting marker.
The Windows Trek font renders that marker as a stray percent sign. Strip it
at read time only at the beginning of a file or line, preserving the original
disc data and any occurrence within actual text.
---
 engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp
index 76a2cccf..c7bbb7cf 100644
--- a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp
@@ -555,6 +555,19 @@ void FileIO::m_readFile(int nargs) {
 		ch = me->_inStream->readByte();
 	}
 
+	// Trek Tech article paragraphs can begin with a legacy 0xA5 formatting
+	// marker. The bundled Windows font renders it as a stray percent sign.
+	// Strip only markers at the beginning of the file or immediately after a
+	// carriage return, leaving the original disc data and real text untouched.
+	if (Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech")) {
+		for (uint i = 0; i < res.size();) {
+			if ((byte)res[i] == 0xA5 && (i == 0 || res[i - 1] == '\r'))
+				res.deleteChar(i);
+			else
+				++i;
+		}
+	}
+
 	g_lingo->push(res);
 }
 
